```

---

# Script Explanation

## Shebang Line

```bash
#!/bin/bash
```

Tells Linux to execute the script using the Bash shell.

---

## User Input

```bash
read -p "Enter your name: " username
```

* `read` → takes input from user
* `-p` → displays prompt message
* `username` → variable storing input

---

## Read Config File

```bash
cat /home/amya/webapp/config/app.conf
```

Displays configuration file content.

---

## Append Log Entry

```bash
echo "Login: $username Date: $(date)" >> /home/amya/webapp/logs/app.log
```

* `echo` → prints text
* `$username` → user-entered name
* `$(date)` → current system date and time
* `>>` → appends output to file

---

## Display Log File

```bash
cat /home/amya/webapp/logs/app.log
```

Displays all log entries.

---

# Final Structure

```text
webapp/
├── scripts/
│   └── log_user.sh
├── logs/
│   └── app.log
└── config/
    └── app.conf
```

